# into this file.
# Added here: Yuka Screwspigot (4324).
# Moved out (0.3.6 flow pass): the Eastern Plaguelands and Darrowshire (Augustus, Terrordale, Light's Hope Chapel,
# Pamela's doll, Zaeldarr, Marlene and Chromie): their ground is level 54-57 and this guide ends about 52.4. Terrordale
# (6164, A Plague Upon Thee's termites) is done on 50-60/05's Egan stop; Darrowshire, Light's Hope Chapel and the
# Marlene/Chromie chain open 50-60/05 at about 56.
# Left out for the level (their targets or ground over level + 2 here, and no later visit that fits): Invader's Scourgestones (5509).
# 0.4.0 level tidy (mobs 2+ over the player done where they fit): Beware of Pterrordax's Frenzied Pterrordax (4501.2,
# 51-54) are killed on the pylon loop at about 52, its Pterrordax (50-52) on the first loop; Pawn Captures Queen (4507)
# is taken on 50-60/05's Gadgetzan stop and worked on 50-60/06's Un'Goro loop; A Plague Upon Thee (5901) is taken at
# the Bulwark on 50-60/04 and worked on 50-60/05's Terrordale stop. Super Sticky (4504) stays on the first loop: its tar drops from the Tar
# Beasts (50-51) and Creepers (51-52) too. The Rise of the Machines (4061, War Reavers 53-55) is left out (no later
# Burning Steppes visit). A short top-up to 51 on Larion's Threshers (only below 51) opens the crater, in place of the
# three small grinds it had; the Trappers and Gorishi (52-53) get Careful tips. Krom'Grul (3822, level 54 alone in his
# caves) is offered from level 53, with no top-up for it. Bungle in the Jungle (4496) needs March of the Silithid from
# 40-50/06 (level 50); without it, 50-60/04-06 take both later. The Jediga deliveries moved to 50-60/04 (Andron Gant
# there).

step Un'Goro Crater
  zone Un'Goro Crater
  goto 41.9,2.7 "Marshal's Refuge"
# Built from the playthrough simulator's consensus route (Horde, visits
# 65-69) and machine-checked with lint; not play-tested on Forever yet.
#
# Flow: Broken Pillar -> down into Un'Goro Crater -> Marshal's Refuge (flight
# path) -> loop 1, anticlockwise: tar pits, the western jungle, the
# south-west, the Gorishi hive, the raft, Torwa, the eastern jungle, the
# gorillas, Fire Plume Ridge (Ringo) -> escort Ringo to the refuge -> loop 2:
# northern pylon, eastern pylon, Lar'korwi, Torwa, western pylon, Krakle,
# Fire Plume Ridge's vent, Krakle -> refuge -> hearth to Gadgetzan -> fly to
# Orgrimmar (Hunters and Shamans train; Druids train in Thunder Bluff on the
# way), zeppelin to Grom'gol, fly to Kargath -> ride through Blackrock
# Mountain to Flame Crest (flight path) -> broodlings -> Dreadmaul Rock ->
# Thaurissan dig site -> Flame Crest -> fly to Kargath -> fly to the
# Undercity (training for the other classes) -> the Bulwark -> ride
# east into the Western Plaguelands: Janice Felstone and the Scarlet
# forward camp, where the next guide starts.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Un'Goro is two loops: Torwa's chain is picked up before the gorillas so
#   their parts drop on the first pass, and Lar'korwi's bait waits for the
#   second loop, which passes his lair and Torwa again. J.D. Collie's crystals
#   are gathered on the first loop.
# - Finding the Source (974) needs level 51, which loop 1 starts below: Krakle
#   is visited on loop 2 instead, with a ride east to Fire Plume Ridge's vent
#   and back (about three minutes), instead of a grind before loop 1.
# - Dropped: The Mighty U'cha (4301): U'cha lives in the north-east cave and
#   Torwa in the south-east corner, so it costs two extra crossings of the
#   crater for 5,650 XP.
# - Grind: the top-up to 52 opens the crater (see the note at the top).
# - Bungle in the Jungle (4496) is turned in when the hearth lands in Gadgetzan
#   instead of on a later Tanaris visit.
# - The Kargath bind is dropped (replaced unused); the Light's Hope Chapel
#   bind is made on arrival there, not in the Badlands.
# - The Undercity and Bulwark stops of the previous guide's export (visits
#   56, 60, 61) are made here, on the way to the Plaguelands: A Call to Arms
#   (5094), Seeping Corruption (3568), Scarlet Diversions (5096), Argent Dawn
#   Commission (5405) and the Bulwark's Scourgestones (5407, 5408). A Call to
#   Arms is handed in on the spot.
# - The Plaguelands beyond the Scarlet camp wait for the later guides (see
#   the note at the top).
# - Dropped: The Rise of the Machines part 2 (4062: a detour to Lotwil for
#   1,350 XP), Dark Iron Legacy (3801: Franclorn is a ghost only a dead
#   character can see), Vivian Lagrave (4133: not taken, see the previous
#   guide) and Yuka Screwspigot (4324).
# - Optional: the Scourgestone turn-ins (5407, 5408, 5509, 5510). They are
#   repeatable Argent Dawn turn-ins and need 20 Minion's or 10 Invader's
#   Scourgestones each, which only drop while the Argent Dawn Commission is
#   equipped; hand them in whenever you have enough.
# - Back at Marshal's Refuge, Shizzle at the entrance first; in the
#   Undercity, Harbinger Balthazad beside the bat master first.
#
# Blackrock Depths (`when dungeon "Blackrock Depths"`, dungeons in the route): for a character who runs it,
# Kargath's WANTED poster gives KILL ON SIGHT: Dark Iron Dwarves (4081) on the first Kargath stop, at about 51; the
# run follows on the way through Blackrock Mountain to the Burning Steppes (the portal is down the walkways from
# the bridge the route crosses), and Warlord Goretooth takes it on the last Kargath stop (`when complete`). Left
# out: its follow-up poster (4082, offered once 4081 is handed in), Thunderheart's quests (3906 first: Overmaster
# Pyron, outside the dungeon; 3907, 3981, 7201 after it), Lost Thunderbrew Recipe (4134: after Vivian Lagrave,
# 4133, not taken), The Heart of the Mountain and Ribbly Screwspigot (4123, 4136: Maxwort Uberglint and Yuka
# Screwspigot at Flame Crest, after the mountain), The Rise of the Machines (4063: after 4062, dropped above) and
# the quests that start inside.
#
# Left open for later guides: The New Springs (980) and It's a Secret to
# Everybody (3908, Donova Snowden), Marvon's Workshop (4147), Felnok
# Steelspring (4808, Everlook), Scarlet Diversions (5096), Seeping
# Corruption (3568), Bone-Bladed Weapons (4300) and Un'Goro Soil (3761).
#
# Left out (not in the route): Dadanga is Hungry! (5150) and the pylon buffs
# (4381-4386, no experience), Chasing A-Me 01 parts 2-3 (Engineering).
#
# Checked and not added: The Mighty U'cha (4301) is still out (see above).
# Linken's Adventure (3961) needs Aquementas (4005), the end of Linken's
# Felwood and Tanaris chain, which no guide does before here. Target:
# Writhing Haunt and its return (5233, 5234) and Mission Accomplished! (5238)
# need the earlier cauldrons (5229-5232, 5235-5236). The route only starts the
# cauldrons in the next guide and finishes them at 58.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Marshal's Refuge

step Into Un'Goro Crater
  tip From the Broken Pillar ride west to the long ramp that winds down into Un'Goro Crater, then follow the crater's north wall to Marshal's Refuge, a camp in the cliff caves. Everyone here is neutral.
  getfp "Marshal's Refuge"
  accept 4284                         -- J.D. Collie, at the back of the cave; below ground
  accept 3882                         -- Spark Nilminer
  accept 3883                         -- Hol'anyee Marshal
  accept 3881                         -- Williden Marshal
  accept 4145                         -- Larion
  accept 4501                         -- the wooden sign beside Spraggle Frock, by the flight master: the Frenzied Pterrordax (51-54) come on the pylon loop

step Out of the refuge
  accept 4503                         -- Shizzle, at the refuge entrance
  accept 4243                         -- Karna Remtravel, just outside
  note From here on pick up every Power Crystal (blue, green, red, yellow) and every Un'Goro Soil pile you pass: 20 for Hamuul, and 5 more for Pestlezugg if you carry Bungle in the Jungle.

step Lakkari Tar Pits
  tip The tar pits lie just south of the refuge. Tar Beasts, Lurkers and Creepers drop the Super Sticky Tar. Careful: the Lurkers reach 54 and the Tar Lords stand among them: take the Tar Beasts (50-51) and Creepers (51-52).
  collect 11834 quest 4504

step Level 51
  when level<51
  tip Top up here to level 51 before the crater's loop: its Pterrordax and Bloodpetal Flayers are up to level 52. The Bloodpetal Threshers (49-50) on the slopes south-east of the refuge are under your level, and Larion wants five of them. Or, with a group, run the Sunken Temple dungeon or the Maraudon dungeon instead.
  goto 61.1,27.6 map 1449 "Bloodpetal Thresher"
  kill 6511 quest 4145.4
  level 51 grind 6511                  -- grind on Bloodpetal Thresher

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Loop 1: south and south-east

step Pterrordax
  tip Pterrordax (50-52) fly over the east of the crater, from the slopes below the refuge southward; their webbed scales are for Shizzle, and Spraggle's sign wants ten of them. Leave the Frenzied Pterrordax over the west for the pylon loop.
  collect 11831 quest 4503.2
  kill 9166 quest 4501.1

step Power Crystals and soil
  tip The crystal clusters stand all over the crater, many around Fire Plume Ridge. Take a few extra of each colour for the pylons.
  collect 11186 quest 4284.1
  collect 11188 quest 4284.2
  collect 11185 quest 4284.3
  collect 11184 quest 4284.4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Loop 1: west and south-west
step Lakkari Tar Pits: kill these as you meet them
  zone Un'Goro Crater
  tip Ride south-west to Fire Plume Ridge, the volcano in the middle of the crater. Bloodpetal Flayers grow around its foot.
  tip South of the hot springs, Dinosaur Bones lie on the ground among the Stegodons and drop from the Diemetradons nearby, which also carry the scales Shizzle wants. Careful: the Stegodons are elites (52-53): pick the bones up around them, don't pull them; the Elder Diemetradons are 53-55, take the smaller ones. Ravasaurs hunt in packs in the south-west: their claws are for Jes'rimon, and now and then one carries a Mangled Journal (a rare drop: take its quest only if you get one). Avoid Gruff, a level 57 Stegodon.
  tip Ride south-west along the western cliffs. Bloodpetal Trappers grow in the jungle there. Careful: the biggest Trappers are 53: pull them one at a time.
  kill 6510 quest 4145.3
  collect 11114 quest 3882
  collect 11830 quest 4503.1
  kill 6512 quest 4145.2

step Research Equipment
  tip The expedition's lost equipment lies in the south-west jungle.
  collect 11112 quest 3881.2 @38.5,66.1

step The Slithering Scar
  when onquest 4496
  tip Careful: Gorishi Workers that drop below 45% health have a 50% chance to call for help from allies within 25 yd. The Hive Guards (54) and the Queen stand inside the hive: work the Workers and Wasps outside it.
  collect 11837 quest 4496.1

step The Slithering Scar
  use 11132 quest 3883.1 @48.7,85.3 map 1449
  collect 11131 quest 3883 @48.7,85.3

step Stegodons and ravasaurs
